# JShark

## Stack
- Haskell GHC 9.14+, Cabal 3.x, optional Nix (`flake.nix`)
- Typed JS EDSL; codegen to JavaScript. Dev server: Scotty (`cabal run examples`)
- Lucid DOM: `jshark-lucid`. Tests need Bun on PATH for JS-vs-interpreter checks
- Ancillary: JS in `examples/Life/js/`, Zig WASM in `examples/Life/wasm/`
- Format: Fourmolu (`fourmolu.yaml`). Test: Tasty + HUnit. Bench: tasty-bench

## Architecture
- PHOAS EDSL: closed terms `forall f`; substitution = Haskell function application
- `Expr` = pure kernel + `Std` stdlib; `Effect` = statements, FFI, DOM, mutation, I/O
- `Arg`/`Rec` join Expr and Effect at FFI; emit via `JShark.Compiler`
- Pure optimizer/codegen paths; push IO (filesystem, network, Scotty) to edges
- `newtype` wrappers for domain primitives; no `head`/`tail`/`fromJust`/`read` in prod
- Recoverable errors: `Either`/`ExceptT`; `error` only for impossible invariants

## Layout
- `src/JShark/` — core library (Api, Compiler, Prim, Dom, Canvas, …)
- `jshark-lucid/` — Lucid integration
- `examples/{Breakout,Life,Synth,TodoMvc,server,static}/`
- `test/`, `bench/`

## Formatting (Fourmolu — strict)
- 2-space indent, 80 cols, leading commas & import/export style
- Leading function arrows; `single-constraint-parens: never`; `unicode: never`
- `scripts/format.sh` or `fourmolu -i ./src ./examples ./test ./jshark-lucid`

## Build
- `cabal build` | `cabal test` | `cabal run examples` (http://localhost:3000)
- Library: `-Wall -Wextra -Werror`; match existing extensions and module conventions
